 "title": "10 ChatGPT Commands to Learn Anything Faster",
 "topic": "ai tools",
 "summary": "The creator shares 10 specific ChatGPT prompt commands designed to help users learn, study, and retain information faster. These commands direct ChatGPT to explain concepts simply, generate visual mind maps or sticky notes, quiz the user, or teach using Socratic questioning.",
 "key_points": [
  "Use 'ELI5' to get ChatGPT to explain any topic in plain, super simple terms.",
  "Use '80/20' to focus ChatGPT on the key 20% of a topic that delivers most of the understanding.",
  "Use 'MAKE-STICKY-NOTES' to turn key facts into visual sticky note guides.",
  "Use 'FEYNMAN-TECHNIQUE' to simplify complex ideas and highlight gaps in understanding.",
  "Use 'MAKE-MINDMAP' to generate visual maps connecting main concepts.",
  "Use 'QUIZME' to have ChatGPT ask questions one at a time to test your knowledge.",
  "Use 'MAKE-VISUAL-STUDYGUIDE' to turn a topic into a concise one-page study sheet.",
  "Use 'FIRSTPRINCIPLES' to break down a topic into its fundamental base ideas.",
  "Use 'SOCRATES' to learn interactively through questions instead of direct answers.",
  "Use 'MAKE-SCHEMATIC' to generate visual schematic diagrams of parts and processes."
 ],
 "content": "Post Text:\nComment CODES for more study commands 👇\n\nStop asking AI for answers.\n\nUse these 10 commands to study, recall, and explain a topic. Put your topic after the command and add your notes if available.\n\n1. ELI5\nExplain the topic in plain words.\n\n2. 80/20\nStart with the most useful 20% of the topic.\n\n3. MAKE-STICKY-NOTES\nTurn the key facts into a sticky note guide.\n\n4. FEYNMAN-TECHNIQUE\nExplain it simply until gaps stand out.\n\n5. MAKE-MINDMAP\nMap the main ideas and their connections.\n\n6. QUIZME\nAsk 1 question at a time.\n\n7. MAKE-VISUAL-STUDYGUIDE\nCreate a 1-page study sheet.\n\n8. FIRSTPRINCIPLES\nBreak the topic into its base ideas.\n\n9. SOCRATES\nTeach through questions instead of a quick answer.\n\n10. MAKE-SCHEMATIC\nDraw a schematic of the parts and how they fit.\n\nChoose 1 command, add a topic, and keep asking questions until you explain it yourself.\n\nWhich ChatGPT prompts help me study?\nHow do I use ChatGPT to learn faster?\nWhat is the Socrates prompt?\n\n#chatgptprompts #chatgpt #ai #aitools #learning\n\nTranscript:\n10 ways to learn anything fast. Number 1: ELI5. Type this anywhere and Chat will explain things in super simple terms. Number 2: 80/20. You can type this anywhere in the prompt and Chat will focus on the most important 20% you need to know. Number 3: MAKE-STICKY-NOTES. ChatGPT will create a visual sticky note guide like this. Number 4: FEYNMAN-TECHNIQUE. Type this anywhere, it's a super popular study technique so that you can learn faster. Number 5: MAKE-MINDMAP. ChatGPT will make a visual mind map of the key concepts. Number 6: QUIZME. Chat will quiz you one question at a time until you understand. Number 7: MAKE-VISUAL-STUDYGUIDE. ChatGPT will take the topic and create a one-pager study sheet so that you can learn everything you need. Number 8: FIRSTPRINCIPLES. Type this anywhere in your prompt and Chat will explain from first principles thinking. Number 9: SOCRATES. This is my favorite. ChatGPT will teach you by asking you questions one at a time. Number 10: MAKE-SCHEMATIC. Type this anywhere and Chat will make a schematic diagram to explain things to you. If you want hundreds more secret codes like this, hit follow and comment CODES and I'll DM you.\n\nOn-screen text:\n- Learn Anything So Fast it's Unfair 🤫\n- #1 ELI5\n- #2 80/20\n- #3 MAKE-STICKY-NOTES\n- #4 FEYNMAN-TECHNIQUE\n- #5 MAKE-MINDMAP\n- #6 QUIZME\n- #7 MAKE-VISUAL-STUDYGUIDE\n- #8 FIRSTPRINCIPLES\n- #9 SOCRATES\n- #10 MAKE-SCHEMATIC\n- Follow me comment \"CODES\" share/repost for priority IG/FB only",
